### 14. Recommended immediate continuation

I recommend treating the next development milestone as:

HyperspaceMapper v2.0 — Computational Core, Release 0.1

The first release should contain only:

- Synthetic experimental-space generator.
- Delaunay tessellation.
- Boundary detection.
- Gaussian-process regression.
- GP-UCB acquisition.
- Combined acquisition function.
- Reproducible benchmarking.
- Unit tests and technical documentation.

Do not integrate physical hardware, Raman/NIR instruments or CFD at this stage. Establish the numerical validity of the central algorithm first.

This will produce a demonstrable computational contribution, a defensible scientific benchmark and a foundation for subsequent sensor-field-informed control.

The immediate next action should be to formalize and implement the Delaunay + GP-UCB computational core, while independently bringing the annotated ChemRobots manuscript to a submission-quality state.
